---
description: Image-to-3D sculpting measured against the image: front maps, registered views, visual hull, map-fitting passes, Blender replay
globs: **/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

Copy this file into your project's `.cursor/rules/`. Install the skill too (Cursor reads `~/.cursor/skills`,
`~/.claude/skills` and `.agents/skills`), so the rule can point at it.

- Use the `image-to-sculpt` skill: scaffold a case with `scripts/i2s.py new`, then `prep`, `views`, `hull`, `fit`,
  `check`, `blender`, `film`, `report` (or `run`).
- Never trust a generated view's requested angle; register it over the whole circle and screen it.
- The photo governs the surfaces it sees; generated views only fill in; their depth is never used.
- Record every step; show the map sheet at every checkpoint; report the held-out view separately.
